{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M3EFt8HJgdCYCQEx1YwWfE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Charging the Regions Victoria EV fast charger network app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Best ways to charge your EV in Melbourne and Victoria\",\"url\":\"https://www.racv.com.au/royalauto/transport/electric-vehicles/where-to-charge-an-electric-car.html\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging & Parking\",\"url\":\"https://www.victoria.ca/getting-around/parking/ev-charging-parking\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle Charging\",\"url\":\"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations VIC - Find Chargers Near You\",\"url\":\"https://plugroo.com.au/vic\"},{\"title\":\"Charging the Regions\",\"url\":\"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions.html\"},{\"title\":\"Regional Victorian Councils Go Public With EV Charger Strategy\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/regional-victoria-ev-charging/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Melbourne\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/melbourne-vic/\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria, British Columbia EV Charging Stations Info\",\"url\":\"https://chargehub.com/en/countries/canada/british-columbia/victoria.html\"},{\"title\":\"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-3\"}]\n\nThe search shows that Charging the Regions chargers run on the **Evie Networks app**.\n\n- **What the program is:** Charging the Regions (CTR) is a long-running program to speed up the rollout of public EV charging in regional Victoria. It is led by the CVGA (Central Victorian Greenhouse Alliance). The program's planning stage was run on behalf of 43 regional councils, 11 metropolitan councils, several greenhouse alliances and the Electric Vehicle Council, with funding from Victoria's environment department (DELWP).\n- **The network:** In Stage 2b, the implementation stage that ran from 2022 to 2024, the program installed 23 fast-charging stations from Whittlesea to Mildura to fill gaps in regional charging.\n- **App and operator:** Evie Networks was contracted to operate and maintain the chargers. An old Tesla Motors Club thread on the CTR network says that the sites were free at the time, according to the Evie app. One of the early sites listed there was in Sale.\n- **Council chargers outside CTR:** Wellington Shire (Gippsland) said its planning drew on the Charging the Regions study. Its council-owned chargers charged 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox app, depending on the location. That page is about 4 years old, so the price may have changed.\n- **Other apps that may help:** Across Victoria, Chargefox and Evie are the main fast-charging providers. Since the two integrated in early 2026, the Chargefox app also covers bp pulse chargers. PlugShare and Plugroo show chargers from all networks on one map.\n\nNone of the results gives the current CTR price per kWh. A CVGA or Evie source would be the place to confirm it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"a24b79c0-db0f-46b0-b39c-1bb35d506b4f","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:38.147Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Charging the Regions Victoria EV fast charger network app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015Yjd5WDcTeNieQ5gW8QVjH","content":[{"title":"Best ways to charge your EV in Melbourne and Victoria","url":"https://www.racv.com.au/royalauto/transport/electric-vehicles/where-to-charge-an-electric-car.html"},{"title":"EV Charging & Parking","url":"https://www.victoria.ca/getting-around/parking/ev-charging-parking"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle Charging","url":"https://www.wellington.vic.gov.au/environment/electric-vehicle-charging"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations VIC - Find Chargers Near You","url":"https://plugroo.com.au/vic"},{"title":"Charging the Regions","url":"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions.html"},{"title":"Regional Victorian Councils Go Public With EV Charger Strategy","url":"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/regional-victoria-ev-charging/"},{"title":"EV Charging & Roadside Assistance in Melbourne","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/locations/melbourne-vic/"},{"title":"Victoria, British Columbia EV Charging Stations Info","url":"https://chargehub.com/en/countries/canada/british-columbia/victoria.html"},{"title":"Victoria Charging the Regions EV network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/victoria-charging-the-regions-ev-network.203235/page-3"}]},"The search shows that Charging the Regions chargers run on the **Evie Networks app**.\n\n- **What the program is:** Charging the Regions (CTR) is a long-running program to speed up the rollout of public EV charging in regional Victoria. It is led by the CVGA (Central Victorian Greenhouse Alliance). The program's planning stage was run on behalf of 43 regional councils, 11 metropolitan councils, several greenhouse alliances and the Electric Vehicle Council, with funding from Victoria's environment department (DELWP).\n- **The network:** In Stage 2b, the implementation stage that ran from 2022 to 2024, the program installed 23 fast-charging stations from Whittlesea to Mildura to fill gaps in regional charging.\n- **App and operator:** Evie Networks was contracted to operate and maintain the chargers. An old Tesla Motors Club thread on the CTR network says that the sites were free at the time, according to the Evie app. One of the early sites listed there was in Sale.\n- **Council chargers outside CTR:** Wellington Shire (Gippsland) said its planning drew on the Charging the Regions study. Its council-owned chargers charged 40c/kWh, paid through either the Evie or Chargefox app, depending on the location. That page is about 4 years old, so the price may have changed.\n- **Other apps that may help:** Across Victoria, Chargefox and Evie are the main fast-charging providers. Since the two integrated in early 2026, the Chargefox app also covers bp pulse chargers. PlugShare and Plugroo show chargers from all networks on one map.\n\nNone of the results gives the current CTR price per kWh. A CVGA or Evie source would be the place to confirm it."],"durationSeconds":8.540075364,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M3EFt8HJgdCYCQEx1YwWfE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gVXviwsWqyjMgbvqJWW94","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Queensland Electric Super Highway how to pay app price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro\",\"url\":\"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging in Public SEQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.jtelectricalcontractors.com.au/ev-charging-in-public-seq\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/\"},{\"title\":\"Welcome to the Living Smart Program\",\"url\":\"https://www.livingsmartqld.com.au/articles/energy/where-to-charge-your-ev\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland to add 18 new EV chargers to take 'electric super highway' inland\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2021/06/17/queensland-to-add-18-new-ev-chargers-to-take-electric-super-highway-inland/\"},{\"title\":\"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/\"}]\n\nPayment runs through the Chargefox app, but the newest price I found (20c/kWh) dates from 2020–2021, so today's rate may be different.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- In 2019 Chargefox took over running the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH). That meant drivers can use one app to find, use and pay for electric car charging locations on the east coast.\n- New sites rolled out by Yurika will be able to be accessed via a smartphone app from Chargefox.\n- A 2021 article said Chargefox and its partner Yurika continue to operate and service the network.\n- A general Queensland guide says some stations accept card payments during charging, while others might require a dedicated app like Chargefox.\n\n**Price per kWh (in date order):**\n- 2019: the network had been free, and reports said a fee of 45 cents per kiloWatt (kW) hour was coming. The minister said they were negotiating a lower price, and prices on Queensland's electric super highway are reportedly set by Yurika Energy.\n- January 2020: a 20c/kWh fee was introduced for electric vehicle drivers using the QESH.\n- June 2021: still 20 cents per kWh, making the network one of the cheaper charging options currently available in Australia.\n- About 2024: a Living Smart QLD page lists a QESH-related site at 90 Sippy Downs Drive with 7kW chargers at $0.30 per kWh. That's AC charging, so it may not reflect fast-charger prices.\n\n**Network status:** a 2025 source says the network of 54 fast charging locations is now fully completed, connecting EV drivers across coastal and inland routes.\n\nNone of these results confirm today's price or whether Chargefox still runs the network. A follow-up search like \"Chargefox QESH price 2026\" or the Queensland Transport and Main Roads QESH page should confirm both.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"3624ae44-6ebf-4653-9bbc-350aba250a82","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:38.340Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Queensland Electric Super Highway how to pay app price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HGRs84pkyHMRkm3zRzPVXN","content":[{"title":"Queensland EV charging no longer free - Servopro","url":"https://servopro.com.au/queensland-ev-charging-no-longer-free/"},{"title":"Electric car drivers can now use Chargefox network from Adelaide to Cairns","url":"https://thedriven.io/2019/07/02/electric-car-drivers-can-now-use-chargefox-network-from-adelaide-to-cairns/"},{"title":"Queensland extends the Electric Super Highway - electrive.com","url":"https://www.electrive.com/2021/06/21/queensland-extends-the-electric-super-highway/"},{"title":"Electric dreaming: Discover the 109 EV charging stations in Queensland - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/exploring-ev-charging-stations-in-queensland"},{"title":"EV Charging in Public SEQ","url":"https://www.jtelectricalcontractors.com.au/ev-charging-in-public-seq"},{"title":"Queensland identifies two more sites for $2.5million EV network rollout","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/02/17/queensland-identifies-two-more-sites-for-2-5million-ev-network-rollout/"},{"title":"Welcome to the Living Smart Program","url":"https://www.livingsmartqld.com.au/articles/energy/where-to-charge-your-ev"},{"title":"Queensland to add 18 new EV chargers to take 'electric super highway' inland","url":"https://thedriven.io/2021/06/17/queensland-to-add-18-new-ev-chargers-to-take-electric-super-highway-inland/"},{"title":"Queensland to add 13 charging stations to Electric Vehicle Super Highway - The Driven","url":"https://thedriven.io/2020/09/10/queensland-to-add-13-charging-stations-to-electric-vehicle-super-highway/"}]},"Payment runs through the Chargefox app, but the newest price I found (20c/kWh) dates from 2020–2021, so today's rate may be different.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- In 2019 Chargefox took over running the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH). That meant drivers can use one app to find, use and pay for electric car charging locations on the east coast.\n- New sites rolled out by Yurika will be able to be accessed via a smartphone app from Chargefox.\n- A 2021 article said Chargefox and its partner Yurika continue to operate and service the network.\n- A general Queensland guide says some stations accept card payments during charging, while others might require a dedicated app like Chargefox.\n\n**Price per kWh (in date order):**\n- 2019: the network had been free, and reports said a fee of 45 cents per kiloWatt (kW) hour was coming. The minister said they were negotiating a lower price, and prices on Queensland's electric super highway are reportedly set by Yurika Energy.\n- January 2020: a 20c/kWh fee was introduced for electric vehicle drivers using the QESH.\n- June 2021: still 20 cents per kWh, making the network one of the cheaper charging options currently available in Australia.\n- About 2024: a Living Smart QLD page lists a QESH-related site at 90 Sippy Downs Drive with 7kW chargers at $0.30 per kWh. That's AC charging, so it may not reflect fast-charger prices.\n\n**Network status:** a 2025 source says the network of 54 fast charging locations is now fully completed, connecting EV drivers across coastal and inland routes.\n\nNone of these results confirm today's price or whether Chargefox still runs the network. A follow-up search like \"Chargefox QESH price 2026\" or the Queensland Transport and Main Roads QESH page should confirm both."],"durationSeconds":9.230125413,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017gVXviwsWqyjMgbvqJWW94","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBTfYkwU2QMKaiCN1HdFxZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RAA EV fast charging network South Australia app price per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"RAA's South Australian EV Charging Network Completed\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/raa-sa-ev-charging-mb3220/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA (SA) Roadside Assistance for EV Owners\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/providers/raa-ev/\"},{\"title\":\"Australia's Best Public EV Charging Station: And The Winner Is ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/best-ev-charging-station-mb3044/\"},{\"title\":\"Discover EV charging stations in South Australia — and drive with confidence - Flare\",\"url\":\"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/19710-2\"},{\"title\":\"Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/guides/cost-to-charge-electric-car/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA to create SA’s first electric vehicle charging network - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-to-create-sas-first-electric-vehicle-charging-network/\"},{\"title\":\"Chargefox: Australia's Biggest EV Network\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/chargefox/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"RAA to roll out 140 new EV charging locations in South Australia in $12.4m plan\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2022/02/14/raa-to-roll-out-140-new-ev-charging-locations-in-south-australia-in-12-4m-plan/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"}]\n\nRAA Charge DC fast charging costs about 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh in the evening peak in metro Adelaide. It's slightly dearer in the country and outback, and you pay through the Chargefox app. The sources don't all agree, so check the app for the live rate.\n\n**Most recent prices (EVRoadside, about mid-2026, checked August 2026):**\n- **Metro Adelaide:** AC is 33c/kWh off-peak and 40c/kWh in the evening peak; DC is 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh peak.\n- **Country and outback:** Country sites cost 1 to 2 cents more and outback sites 3 to 5 cents more, so across the whole network AC runs 33 to 45 cents and DC 66 to 78 cents.\n- **Peak hours:** the higher rate applies during its 5pm to 10pm evening peak.\n\n**Older prices (SolarQuotes, about 16 months ago):** Rapid (150kW) and ultra-rapid (200kW) sites were Evening peak (5pm-10pm): 73c/kWh; Standard (all other times): 64c/kWh, and destination AC was 30c and 37c. RAA said it was the only network operator in South Australia to have cheaper prices during the day. Another SolarQuotes page, dated 23 days ago, still lists 64c and 73c, so it may be out of date. The 66c and 75c figures look more current.\n\n**App and member discount:**\n- Charging sessions and payments are controlled via the Chargefox app, which also shows where the stations are located.\n- Chargefox states plainly that it does not set the price of charging, and the owner of each station does.\n- RAA members get 10% off by adding their RAA membership number to the Chargefox app. For example, at 75c that saves 7.5 cents a kilowatt hour, or $3.75 on a 50 kWh charge.\n\n**Network background:** RAA Charge has 140+ sites and 550+ plugs from Yalata to Mount Gambier, completed in 2025; over 75% of sites are regional. Its DC sites run 60 to 200 kW. When the network was announced in 2022, RAA expected a flat price of about 35c/kWh.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"8d62c55f-b13c-4db4-81ee-43cc6c6b4264","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:39.735Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"RAA EV fast charging network South Australia app price per kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016m5iAToGreAxfqPmywYSuW","content":[{"title":"RAA's South Australian EV Charging Network Completed","url":"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/raa-sa-ev-charging-mb3220/"},{"title":"RAA (SA) Roadside Assistance for EV Owners","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/providers/raa-ev/"},{"title":"Australia's Best Public EV Charging Station: And The Winner Is ...","url":"https://www.solarquotes.com.au/blog/best-ev-charging-station-mb3044/"},{"title":"Discover EV charging stations in South Australia — and drive with confidence - Flare","url":"https://www.flarehr.com/blog/19710-2"},{"title":"Cost to Charge an Electric Car in Australia","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/guides/cost-to-charge-electric-car/"},{"title":"RAA to create SA’s first electric vehicle charging network - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-to-create-sas-first-electric-vehicle-charging-network/"},{"title":"Chargefox: Australia's Biggest EV Network","url":"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/chargefox/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"RAA to roll out 140 new EV charging locations in South Australia in $12.4m plan","url":"https://thedriven.io/2022/02/14/raa-to-roll-out-140-new-ev-charging-locations-in-south-australia-in-12-4m-plan/"},{"title":"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)","url":"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/"}]},"RAA Charge DC fast charging costs about 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh in the evening peak in metro Adelaide. It's slightly dearer in the country and outback, and you pay through the Chargefox app. The sources don't all agree, so check the app for the live rate.\n\n**Most recent prices (EVRoadside, about mid-2026, checked August 2026):**\n- **Metro Adelaide:** AC is 33c/kWh off-peak and 40c/kWh in the evening peak; DC is 66c/kWh off-peak and 75c/kWh peak.\n- **Country and outback:** Country sites cost 1 to 2 cents more and outback sites 3 to 5 cents more, so across the whole network AC runs 33 to 45 cents and DC 66 to 78 cents.\n- **Peak hours:** the higher rate applies during its 5pm to 10pm evening peak.\n\n**Older prices (SolarQuotes, about 16 months ago):** Rapid (150kW) and ultra-rapid (200kW) sites were Evening peak (5pm-10pm): 73c/kWh; Standard (all other times): 64c/kWh, and destination AC was 30c and 37c. RAA said it was the only network operator in South Australia to have cheaper prices during the day. Another SolarQuotes page, dated 23 days ago, still lists 64c and 73c, so it may be out of date. The 66c and 75c figures look more current.\n\n**App and member discount:**\n- Charging sessions and payments are controlled via the Chargefox app, which also shows where the stations are located.\n- Chargefox states plainly that it does not set the price of charging, and the owner of each station does.\n- RAA members get 10% off by adding their RAA membership number to the Chargefox app. For example, at 75c that saves 7.5 cents a kilowatt hour, or $3.75 on a 50 kWh charge.\n\n**Network background:** RAA Charge has 140+ sites and 550+ plugs from Yalata to Mount Gambier, completed in 2025; over 75% of sites are regional. Its DC sites run 60 to 200 kW. When the network was announced in 2022, RAA expected a flat price of about 35c/kWh."],"durationSeconds":9.729481845,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GBTfYkwU2QMKaiCN1HdFxZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
