{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EXkXGnCJrjs3osmXGpyDyk","type":"tool_result","content":"**Operator:** The page names Evie Networks: \"Evie Networks contracted for operation and maintenance of the installed chargers.\" This refers to the 23 fast-charging stations from Stage 2b.\n\n**Payment app:** The page doesn't say which app drivers use to pay. Evie Networks likely has its own app, but the page doesn't confirm that.\n\n**Price per kWh:** The page gives no charging price or tariff.\n\nFor app and pricing details, you'd need Evie Networks' own materials or the linked media release, which may have more information."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"99e820f8-ab5e-4dff-b208-f9d6a4ca92da","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:46.974Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":39806,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Operator:** The page names Evie Networks: \"Evie Networks contracted for operation and maintenance of the installed chargers.\" This refers to the 23 fast-charging stations from Stage 2b.\n\n**Payment app:** The page doesn't say which app drivers use to pay. Evie Networks likely has its own app, but the page doesn't confirm that.\n\n**Price per kWh:** The page gives no charging price or tariff.\n\nFor app and pricing details, you'd need Evie Networks' own materials or the linked media release, which may have more information.","durationMs":4002,"url":"https://www.cvga.org.au/charging-the-regions.html"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EXkXGnCJrjs3osmXGpyDyk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AZ24z1wuiQ9rBFtqsBhjZA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:qld.gov.au electric super highway Chargefox app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging decommissioning and new location\",\"url\":\"https://www.yoursay.edq.qld.gov.au/northshore/ev-charging-relocation-2\"},{\"title\":\"EV Station in Goondiwindi Boosts the Electric Super Highway\",\"url\":\"https://www.grc.qld.gov.au/News-and-Events/News/Council-News/2023/EV-Station-in-Goondiwindi-Boosts-the-Electric-Super-Highway\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle snapshot March 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-march-2024\"},{\"title\":\"Road Conditions and Fuel Supplies\",\"url\":\"https://www.winton.qld.gov.au/News/Road-Conditions\"},{\"title\":\"Tropical North charged with electric vehicle pilot project - Ministerial Media Statements\",\"url\":\"https://statements.qld.gov.au/statements/87725\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle snapshot (Department of Transport and Main Roads)\",\"url\":\"https://www.tmr.qld.gov.au/community-and-environment/electric-vehicles/electric-vehicle-snapshot\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle snapshot October 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-october-2023\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicle snapshot June 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-june-2024\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles and charging (Department of Transport and Main Roads)\",\"url\":\"https://www.tmr.qld.gov.au/community-and-environment/electric-vehicles/electric-vehicles-and-charging\"},{\"title\":\"Address all correspondence to: Chief Executive Officer\",\"url\":\"https://www.longreach.qld.gov.au/files/assets/public/v/1/about-council/documents/meeting-minutes-and-agendas/2023_05_18_council_agenda.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search turned up several Queensland government and council pages that link the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH) to Chargefox:\n\n- **Who runs it:** Yurika owns and operates all fast charging stations along the QESH. The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) calls Chargefox the charge point operator for the Queensland Electric Super Highway network, and its usage figures come from Chargefox.\n- **Using the app:** Goondiwindi Regional Council tells drivers to download the Chargefox app to find and use charging stations as well as to make convenient payments. Winton Shire Council says its site offers a 75kW DC fast charger (Tritium RTM) and a 22kW AC charger (Siemens) operated via the Chargefox app.\n- **Prices:** On 1 March 2024, the rate for 50kW and 75kW chargers at QESH sites went up from 30 cents to 55 cents per kilowatt-hour. The 22kW chargers stayed at 30 cents. Before that, a $0.20/kWh charge was introduced on 28 January 2020.\n- **Site change:** The temporary QESH charging site at 281 MacArthur Avenue, Northshore Brisbane, was to be decommissioned from 25 May 2024 to make way for the Bluey's World attraction. EV users were told they would get more information through the Chargefox app.\n- **Phase 3:** This stage was set to add an extra 24 locations to the network, on routes such as Goondiwindi to Emerald and Longreach to Cairns.\n- **Ownership:** A 2023 Longreach Council agenda mentions the NRMA's acquisition of Chargefox.\n\nMost of these pages are from 2023–2024, so the prices and site details may be out of date. The two TMR pages were updated more recently, about six months ago.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"aa694467-faa4-4a1b-8171-2274629bc699","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:51.793Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:qld.gov.au electric super highway Chargefox app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012avoFFqeaSFQPqmxxCBFJP","content":[{"title":"EV charging decommissioning and new location","url":"https://www.yoursay.edq.qld.gov.au/northshore/ev-charging-relocation-2"},{"title":"EV Station in Goondiwindi Boosts the Electric Super Highway","url":"https://www.grc.qld.gov.au/News-and-Events/News/Council-News/2023/EV-Station-in-Goondiwindi-Boosts-the-Electric-Super-Highway"},{"title":"Electric vehicle snapshot March 2024","url":"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-march-2024"},{"title":"Road Conditions and Fuel Supplies","url":"https://www.winton.qld.gov.au/News/Road-Conditions"},{"title":"Tropical North charged with electric vehicle pilot project - Ministerial Media Statements","url":"https://statements.qld.gov.au/statements/87725"},{"title":"Electric vehicle snapshot (Department of Transport and Main Roads)","url":"https://www.tmr.qld.gov.au/community-and-environment/electric-vehicles/electric-vehicle-snapshot"},{"title":"Electric vehicle snapshot October 2023","url":"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-october-2023"},{"title":"Electric vehicle snapshot June 2024","url":"https://www.qld.gov.au/transport/projects/electricvehicles/zero-emission-strategy/electric-vehicle-snapshot-june-2024"},{"title":"Electric vehicles and charging (Department of Transport and Main Roads)","url":"https://www.tmr.qld.gov.au/community-and-environment/electric-vehicles/electric-vehicles-and-charging"},{"title":"Address all correspondence to: Chief Executive Officer","url":"https://www.longreach.qld.gov.au/files/assets/public/v/1/about-council/documents/meeting-minutes-and-agendas/2023_05_18_council_agenda.pdf"}]},"The search turned up several Queensland government and council pages that link the Queensland Electric Super Highway (QESH) to Chargefox:\n\n- **Who runs it:** Yurika owns and operates all fast charging stations along the QESH. The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) calls Chargefox the charge point operator for the Queensland Electric Super Highway network, and its usage figures come from Chargefox.\n- **Using the app:** Goondiwindi Regional Council tells drivers to download the Chargefox app to find and use charging stations as well as to make convenient payments. Winton Shire Council says its site offers a 75kW DC fast charger (Tritium RTM) and a 22kW AC charger (Siemens) operated via the Chargefox app.\n- **Prices:** On 1 March 2024, the rate for 50kW and 75kW chargers at QESH sites went up from 30 cents to 55 cents per kilowatt-hour. The 22kW chargers stayed at 30 cents. Before that, a $0.20/kWh charge was introduced on 28 January 2020.\n- **Site change:** The temporary QESH charging site at 281 MacArthur Avenue, Northshore Brisbane, was to be decommissioned from 25 May 2024 to make way for the Bluey's World attraction. EV users were told they would get more information through the Chargefox app.\n- **Phase 3:** This stage was set to add an extra 24 locations to the network, on routes such as Goondiwindi to Emerald and Longreach to Cairns.\n- **Ownership:** A 2023 Longreach Council agenda mentions the NRMA's acquisition of Chargefox.\n\nMost of these pages are from 2023–2024, so the prices and site details may be out of date. The two TMR pages were updated more recently, about six months ago."],"durationSeconds":8.373964609000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AZ24z1wuiQ9rBFtqsBhjZA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7DqQbTYk1CBC7VT8UKyBJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:raa.com.au RAA Charge Chargefox app\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV charging stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"Help Centre\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/help-centre/motoring-services-support/ev-charging-network\"},{\"title\":\"Electric vehicles\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charging Stations - RAA member discount\",\"url\":\"https://our.raa.com.au/membership/member-discounts-and-offers/ev-charging-stations\"},{\"title\":\"RAA\",\"url\":\"https://www.raa.com.au/?q=trip+planner\"},{\"title\":\"RAA Charge closes the gap in SA-WA crossing for EV drivers - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-closes-the-gap-in-sa-wa-crossing-for-ev-drivers/\"},{\"title\":\"More charging sites underway as EV sales increase - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/more-charging-sites-underway-as-ev-sales-increase/\"},{\"title\":\"Five new RAA Charge locations come online amidst a record-breaking March - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/five-new-raa-charge-locations-come-online-amidst-a-record-breaking-march/\"},{\"title\":\"September Surge: Six RAA Charge Rapid and Ultra-Rapid sites go under construction - RAA Daily\",\"url\":\"https://daily.raa.com.au/september-surge-six-raa-charge-rapid-and-ultra-rapid-sites-go-under-construction/\"}]\n\nRAA's own site confirms that RAA Charge, its EV charging network in South Australia, runs on the Chargefox app.\n\n**How it works**\n- You download Chargefox for iOS or Android, find an RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's map, then charge your EV and pay through the Chargefox app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA calls Chargefox its \"platform provider\": \"We are working with our platform provider Chargefox...\"\n- Charging sessions take place via the Chargefox app and are facilitated by Chargefox. For help with the app, RAA tells users to contact Chargefox (via the details in the 'Help & Support' of the app).\n- The app also shows charger availability, receipts and charging history. It lists all locations and charger availability, and you can see receipts and track your charging history in the app.\n\n**RAA member discount (10%)**\n- To get it, members must have logged into the Chargefox app, selected RAA as their member program and added a valid RAA membership number to their profile before charging starts. It can't be activated or applied after a charge session has commenced or has been completed.\n- Member prices per kWh (off-peak / 5–10pm peak): Metro AC 40c/kWh* 33c/kWh* Metro DC 75c/kWh* 66c/kWh* Country AC 42c/kWh* 35c/kWh* Country DC 76c/kWh* 68c/kWh*\n\n**Idle fees (DC rapid sites in SA)**\n- The Chargefox app notifies you when charging is complete. You get a 10-minute grace period, then it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in. These are charged to the credit card linked to your Chargefox account.\n\n**About the network**\n- 530 plugs at more than 140 sites in South Australia, 75% of them in regional areas. It runs on net 100% renewable energy.\n- AC sites (7–22kW) have Type 2 plugs, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached. The Chargefox app shows the plug type for every RAA Charge station.\n\nMain sources: raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations, the RAA Help Centre's EV charging page, and the member discount terms at our.raa.com.au.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"0b8aae99-c25b-471e-b0c8-23f020790cc2","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:29:54.117Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:raa.com.au RAA Charge Chargefox app","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019FrUG5MVQK3VydkY5KyLcM","content":[{"title":"EV charging stations","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"Help Centre","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/help-centre/motoring-services-support/ev-charging-network"},{"title":"Electric vehicles","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/motor/ev-hub"},{"title":"RAA Charging Stations - RAA member discount","url":"https://our.raa.com.au/membership/member-discounts-and-offers/ev-charging-stations"},{"title":"RAA","url":"https://www.raa.com.au/?q=trip+planner"},{"title":"RAA Charge closes the gap in SA-WA crossing for EV drivers - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/media-resources/raa-charge-closes-the-gap-in-sa-wa-crossing-for-ev-drivers/"},{"title":"More charging sites underway as EV sales increase - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/more-charging-sites-underway-as-ev-sales-increase/"},{"title":"Five new RAA Charge locations come online amidst a record-breaking March - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/five-new-raa-charge-locations-come-online-amidst-a-record-breaking-march/"},{"title":"September Surge: Six RAA Charge Rapid and Ultra-Rapid sites go under construction - RAA Daily","url":"https://daily.raa.com.au/september-surge-six-raa-charge-rapid-and-ultra-rapid-sites-go-under-construction/"}]},"RAA's own site confirms that RAA Charge, its EV charging network in South Australia, runs on the Chargefox app.\n\n**How it works**\n- You download Chargefox for iOS or Android, find an RAA Charge site in the app or on RAA's map, then charge your EV and pay through the Chargefox app or with your RFID card.\n- RAA calls Chargefox its \"platform provider\": \"We are working with our platform provider Chargefox...\"\n- Charging sessions take place via the Chargefox app and are facilitated by Chargefox. For help with the app, RAA tells users to contact Chargefox (via the details in the 'Help & Support' of the app).\n- The app also shows charger availability, receipts and charging history. It lists all locations and charger availability, and you can see receipts and track your charging history in the app.\n\n**RAA member discount (10%)**\n- To get it, members must have logged into the Chargefox app, selected RAA as their member program and added a valid RAA membership number to their profile before charging starts. It can't be activated or applied after a charge session has commenced or has been completed.\n- Member prices per kWh (off-peak / 5–10pm peak): Metro AC 40c/kWh* 33c/kWh* Metro DC 75c/kWh* 66c/kWh* Country AC 42c/kWh* 35c/kWh* Country DC 76c/kWh* 68c/kWh*\n\n**Idle fees (DC rapid sites in SA)**\n- The Chargefox app notifies you when charging is complete. You get a 10-minute grace period, then it's $1 per minute if you stay plugged in. These are charged to the credit card linked to your Chargefox account.\n\n**About the network**\n- 530 plugs at more than 140 sites in South Australia, 75% of them in regional areas. It runs on net 100% renewable energy.\n- AC sites (7–22kW) have Type 2 plugs, so you need your own cable. DC sites (60–200kW) have cables attached. The Chargefox app shows the plug type for every RAA Charge station.\n\nMain sources: raa.com.au/motor/motoring-services/ev-charging-stations, the RAA Help Centre's EV charging page, and the member discount terms at our.raa.com.au."],"durationSeconds":10.297326901,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01J7DqQbTYk1CBC7VT8UKyBJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
