{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GCPUbEkwrVLFshJ3rF13Nc","type":"tool_result","content":"README.md:40:| [`prices.md`](.github/workflows/prices.md) | 8th of each month | Finds operators with three or more fast sites that no network matches, decides whether each is a new network, and checks typical prices against sources it may read | `networks.json` |\nREADME.md:73:node scripts/new-operators.mjs chargers.json 3  # operators no network matches, from a charger file\nscripts/lib.mjs:48:    if (passing.length !== 1) errors.push(`${path}: must match exactly one allowed shape`);\nscripts/lib.mjs:56:    if (schema.pattern && !new RegExp(schema.pattern).test(value)) errors.push(`${path}: \"${value}\" doesn't match ${schema.pattern}`);\nscripts/lib.mjs:172:    for (const n of rows) for (const m of n.match) {\nscripts/lib.mjs:173:      if (owners.has(m)) errors.push(`networks: \"${m}\" matches both ${owners.get(m)} and ${n.id}`);\nscripts/lib.mjs:204: * `networks` matches: candidates for a new network.\nscripts/lib.mjs:213:    if (networks.networks.some((n) => n.match.some((m) => text.includes(m)))) continue;\nscripts/new-operators.mjs:3:// network in networks.json matches: candidates for a new network.\nscripts/lib.test.mjs:83:  doc.networks.push({ id: \"newNet\", name: \"New Net\", match: [\"new net\"], typicalPerKWh: null, basis: \"estimate\", siteReading: \"unchecked\", source: \"Seen in the charger file\", checked: \"2026-11-15\" });\nscripts/lib.test.mjs:88:test(\"two networks can't claim the same match text\", () => {\nscripts/lib.test.mjs:90:  doc.networks.push({ id: \"other\", name: \"Other\", match: [\"evie\"], typicalPerKWh: null, basis: \"none\", siteReading: \"unchecked\", source: \"Seen in the charger file\", checked: \"2026-11-15\" });\nscripts/lib.test.mjs:91:  assert.ok(validate(\"networks\", { doc, now }).some((e) => e.includes('\"evie\" matches both')));\n.github/workflows/prices.md:105:- **How to recognise their sit