{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8xfPw9q79pvCHssndQXUF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial\",\"url\":\"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators\"},{\"title\":\"For drivers — how charging works\",\"url\":\"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt - App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"},{\"title\":\"AEVA\",\"url\":\"https://aeva.asn.au/directories/wevolt/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Costs in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt on the App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/lv/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"},{\"title\":\"Wevolt - App Store - Apple\",\"url\":\"https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/wevolt/id6446931550\"}]\n\nWevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger owner sets its own price, so rates differ from site to site.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt is a Perth-based company that runs the app, the network and the payments. The chargers themselves are owned and run by independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. Wevolt's fee (a Service Fee) is added on top of that price.\n- **New fee from 13 Oct 2026:** Wevolt now keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost on paid sessions started through the app or a Wevolt card. This comes out of the operator's payout.\n- **A WA example:** At Transperth's charger trial, Wevolt runs 7kW AC chargers. taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV The price is $0.43 per kWh, which covers the cost of electricity and operating the charger. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Typical ranges (from the MyEVJourney blog, which isn't an official source):**\n  - Jan 2026 table: Wevolt DC | 35 | 73 c/kWh, which works out to about $7.00–$14.60 per 100km.\n  - Dec 2025 table: 45–75c/kWh.\n  - Sept 2025 table: 0–65c/kWh across all Wevolt chargers.\n- **Other costs:** Some DC Idle fees are from 3c to $2/minute. This is a general figure for DC chargers, not specific to Wevolt.\n- **In the app:** You can see live availability and pricing for each charger before starting. When you start a session, a pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"a08a61e3-3fb2-4a99-b786-5ea66dd5b0f7","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:30:32.737Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"WeVolt EV charging Western Australia app price kWh","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MZycxsjpy341g3CRVCX6uA","content":[{"title":"Transperth Electric Vehicle Charger Trial","url":"https://www.mysaytransport.wa.gov.au/pta-ev-chargers"},{"title":"Charging Fees, the Service Fee and the Platform Fee (for Operators) — Wevolt Support","url":"https://wevolt.com.au/support/kb/charging-fees-and-the-service-fee-for-operators"},{"title":"For drivers — how charging works","url":"https://wevolt.com.au/drivers"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2026/01/01/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Wevolt - App Store - Apple","url":"https://apps.apple.com/au/app/wevolt/id6446931550"},{"title":"AEVA","url":"https://aeva.asn.au/directories/wevolt/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/12/23/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Costs in Australia","url":"https://myevjourney.com/2025/09/20/ev-charging-costs-australia/"},{"title":"Wevolt on the App Store - Apple","url":"https://apps.apple.com/lv/app/wevolt/id6446931550"},{"title":"Wevolt - App Store - Apple","url":"https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/wevolt/id6446931550"}]},"Wevolt doesn't have one network-wide price per kWh. Each charger owner sets its own price, so rates differ from site to site.\n\n- **How pricing works:** Wevolt is a Perth-based company that runs the app, the network and the payments. The chargers themselves are owned and run by independent operators — businesses, councils, property owners and workplaces — who list them in the app and set their own prices. Operators can charge per kWh, per minute, as a flat fee, or with a free period, plus any idle fee. Wevolt's fee (a Service Fee) is added on top of that price.\n- **New fee from 13 Oct 2026:** Wevolt now keeps a Platform Fee of 4% of the charging cost on paid sessions started through the app or a Wevolt card. This comes out of the operator's payout.\n- **A WA example:** At Transperth's charger trial, Wevolt runs 7kW AC chargers. taking approximately eight hours to charge a typical EV The price is $0.43 per kWh, which covers the cost of electricity and operating the charger. That page is about 9 months old.\n- **Typical ranges (from the MyEVJourney blog, which isn't an official source):**\n  - Jan 2026 table: Wevolt DC | 35 | 73 c/kWh, which works out to about $7.00–$14.60 per 100km.\n  - Dec 2025 table: 45–75c/kWh.\n  - Sept 2025 table: 0–65c/kWh across all Wevolt chargers.\n- **Other costs:** Some DC Idle fees are from 3c to $2/minute. This is a general figure for DC chargers, not specific to Wevolt.\n- **In the app:** You can see live availability and pricing for each charger before starting. When you start a session, a pre-authorisation hold is placed on your card, then you're billed for the energy used."],"durationSeconds":9.033072964999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R8xfPw9q79pvCHssndQXUF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W21H8vkbuAjLtEGaFnxEGJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Engie EV fast charging Australia app Glen Waverley Box Hill pay\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parking - The Glen\",\"url\":\"https://www.theglen.com.au/centre-info/parking\"},{\"title\":\"Glen Waverley EV Charging Stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.evchargingmap.com.au/victoria/glen-waverley\"},{\"title\":\"EV Chargers Glen Waverley VIC — 3 Stations\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/guides/public-ev-chargers/vic/glen-waverley\"},{\"title\":\"Public EV Charging\",\"url\":\"https://engie.com.au/business/multi-site-business/ev-charging-network/public-ev-charging\"},{\"title\":\"ENGIE EV Flex Charge - Electric Vehicle Energy Plan\",\"url\":\"https://engie.com.au/residential/product/engie-ev-flex-charge\"},{\"title\":\"CDG ENGIE EV Charging FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://cdgengie.com/appinfo/FAQ/\"},{\"title\":\"Destination Charging Across Victoria Program - Energy\",\"url\":\"https://www.energy.vic.gov.au/grants/destination-charging-across-victoria-program\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle Energy Plan\",\"url\":\"https://engie.com.au/residential/energy-efficiency/engie-ev\"},{\"title\":\"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/engie-australian-ev-charging-network.239616/page-3\"},{\"title\":\"Best EV Electricity Plans Australia (Oct 2026): 15 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/best-ev-electricity-plans-australia\"}]\n\nI searched once. The results cover Glen Waverley well but say nothing about an Engie site at Box Hill.\n\n**Glen Waverley (The Glen shopping centre, 235 Springvale Rd)**\n- The Glen lists paid ENGIE fast chargers in the B1 Yellow Car Park, reached via Snedden Drive and Springvale Road.\n- **How you pay:** The chargers run on a pay-per-kWh system via the Exploren and ChargeFox app. The DC fast and AC slow chargers have been upgraded to include the Exploren software platform, but the current Chargefox platform will still be available at DC chargers.\n- **Hardware:** Gridly lists a 100 kW DC fast charger with 4 plugs. A 2021 Tesla Motors Club post listed The Glen with 100kW, 3xCCS 1xChademo.\n- **Typical prices** (a general guide for Glen Waverley, not The Glen's own rates): DC fast charging (50kW) at $0.40–$0.70 per kWh; ultra-rapid DC (350kW) at $0.75–$0.90.\n- The Tesla Motors Club thread is now titled \"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)\", which fits with the network moving from Engie/Chargefox branding to Exploren.\n\n**About Engie's network**\n- Engie's public charging page tells drivers to download the Chargefox App to find stations near you. The network was funded through a $22 million program supported by ARENA through its Future Fuels program.\n- The 2021 thread lists other Melbourne Engie sites: Bayside Centre, Frankston, 120kW, 2xCCS; Victoria Gardens, Richmond, 100kW, 3xCCS, 1xChademo, plus Caribbean Park, where billing was by ChargeFox.\n\n**Gaps:** Nothing in the results confirms an Engie site at Box Hill. To find one, search \"Exploren Box Hill\" or \"Box Hill Central EV charging\". None of the results mention paying by tapping a credit card at the charger, so expect to need either the Exploren or the Chargefox app.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"0fed724f-74ae-4c80-998a-5a6afe13dcbf","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:30:33.313Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Engie EV fast charging Australia app Glen Waverley Box Hill pay","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011L6gwuQCp8sJpPaDmsosmR","content":[{"title":"Parking - The Glen","url":"https://www.theglen.com.au/centre-info/parking"},{"title":"Glen Waverley EV Charging Stations","url":"https://www.evchargingmap.com.au/victoria/glen-waverley"},{"title":"EV Chargers Glen Waverley VIC — 3 Stations","url":"https://www.gridly.com.au/guides/public-ev-chargers/vic/glen-waverley"},{"title":"Public EV Charging","url":"https://engie.com.au/business/multi-site-business/ev-charging-network/public-ev-charging"},{"title":"ENGIE EV Flex Charge - Electric Vehicle Energy Plan","url":"https://engie.com.au/residential/product/engie-ev-flex-charge"},{"title":"CDG ENGIE EV Charging FAQ","url":"https://cdgengie.com/appinfo/FAQ/"},{"title":"Destination Charging Across Victoria Program - Energy","url":"https://www.energy.vic.gov.au/grants/destination-charging-across-victoria-program"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle Energy Plan","url":"https://engie.com.au/residential/energy-efficiency/engie-ev"},{"title":"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/engie-australian-ev-charging-network.239616/page-3"},{"title":"Best EV Electricity Plans Australia (Oct 2026): 15 Compared","url":"https://zecar.com/reviews/best-ev-electricity-plans-australia"}]},"I searched once. The results cover Glen Waverley well but say nothing about an Engie site at Box Hill.\n\n**Glen Waverley (The Glen shopping centre, 235 Springvale Rd)**\n- The Glen lists paid ENGIE fast chargers in the B1 Yellow Car Park, reached via Snedden Drive and Springvale Road.\n- **How you pay:** The chargers run on a pay-per-kWh system via the Exploren and ChargeFox app. The DC fast and AC slow chargers have been upgraded to include the Exploren software platform, but the current Chargefox platform will still be available at DC chargers.\n- **Hardware:** Gridly lists a 100 kW DC fast charger with 4 plugs. A 2021 Tesla Motors Club post listed The Glen with 100kW, 3xCCS 1xChademo.\n- **Typical prices** (a general guide for Glen Waverley, not The Glen's own rates): DC fast charging (50kW) at $0.40–$0.70 per kWh; ultra-rapid DC (350kW) at $0.75–$0.90.\n- The Tesla Motors Club thread is now titled \"Exploren EV charging network (Including Engie)\", which fits with the network moving from Engie/Chargefox branding to Exploren.\n\n**About Engie's network**\n- Engie's public charging page tells drivers to download the Chargefox App to find stations near you. The network was funded through a $22 million program supported by ARENA through its Future Fuels program.\n- The 2021 thread lists other Melbourne Engie sites: Bayside Centre, Frankston, 120kW, 2xCCS; Victoria Gardens, Richmond, 100kW, 3xCCS, 1xChademo, plus Caribbean Park, where billing was by ChargeFox.\n\n**Gaps:** Nothing in the results confirms an Engie site at Box Hill. To find one, search \"Exploren Box Hill\" or \"Box Hill Central EV charging\". None of the results mention paying by tapping a credit card at the charger, so expect to need either the Exploren or the Chargefox app."],"durationSeconds":10.111183067999992,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01W21H8vkbuAjLtEGaFnxEGJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fm9FTohaya2A6vAknMw2B9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Electrona EV charger Tasmania Coles Bay Bicheno app pay\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"electrona.au — EV Charging Station Customer Help Site\",\"url\":\"https://electrona.au/\"},{\"title\":\"electrona.au — BCHNO001 - Electric Vehicle Charge Station - Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania, Australia\",\"url\":\"https://electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html\"},{\"title\":\"Australia’s first tap and go fast charging station up and running\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/04/14/australias-first-tap-and-go-fast-charging-station-up-and-running/\"},{\"title\":\"Bicheno Town Centre\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/494062\"},{\"title\":\"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects\",\"url\":\"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/\"},{\"title\":\"DC fast chargers in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://www.aeva.asn.au/tas/dc-fast-chargers\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Vehicle ChargeSmart Grants\",\"url\":\"https://recfit.tas.gov.au/grants_programs/chargesmart_grants\"},{\"title\":\"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4\"},{\"title\":\"NRMA fast charging network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/nrma-fast-charging-network.100487/page-68\"}]\n\nElectrona's Bicheno charger is open and you can pay by tapping a card, with no app needed. The Coles Bay charger is funded but still marked \"coming soon.\"\n\n**Bicheno (open since April 2023)**\n- **Location:** Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania (near IGA), station ID BCHNO001.\n- **Payment without an app:** You start a charge on the touch screen and pay with your credit card, with no app needed. The terminal takes credit cards, debit cards and NFC devices, but only Visa and Mastercard.\n- **Steps:** Plug a DC cable into the car (or use your own AC cable in the right-hand socket), tap the touch screen, choose \"Card Payment\" and then \"Start Charge\", and tap your card or phone on the reader.\n- **App or RFID backup:** If the card terminal gives you trouble, or you'd rather use an app, Wevolt works as an alternative and is on the App Store and Google Play. An RFID card also works. You can check availability in the Wevolt app or the Charge@Large app.\n- **Pricing (may change):** a $50 pre-authorisation that settles to the amount you actually used once your bank processes it. DC (CCS/CHAdeMO) costs $3 per session plus $0.64 per kWh; AC Type 2 costs $1 per session plus $0.64 per kWh. According to PlugShare, DC charging is capped at 2 hours, and a $0.50/minute idle fee applies after that.\n- **Hardware:** a Circontrol Raption with 50kW DC and 12kW AC, which can charge one car on DC and another on AC Type 2 at the same time.\n\n**Coles Bay (not open yet)**\n- Electrona's website lists Coles Bay and Orford as coming soon.\n- Under the Tasmanian Government's ChargeSmart 3 (2025) grants, Electrona Pty Ltd received $46,000 for Coles Bay. A June 2025 update from Electrona says it is bringing new fast chargers to Port Arthur, Bothwell, Coles Bay, and Orford.\n- I didn't find an opening date or confirmed payment methods for Coles Bay. Electrona's other sites suggest it will probably take cards and Wevolt too, but that isn't confirmed.\n\nElectrona's other open sites are Bothwell, Buckland, Huonville and Port Arthur.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"088cd5be-8cd2-4214-88c2-6bf576201d1d","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:30:35.170Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Electrona EV charger Tasmania Coles Bay Bicheno app pay","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019nC2oYxuvk8NeWRYsFNFVY","content":[{"title":"electrona.au — EV Charging Station Customer Help Site","url":"https://electrona.au/"},{"title":"electrona.au — BCHNO001 - Electric Vehicle Charge Station - Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania, Australia","url":"https://electrona.au/evc/bchno/bchno-001.html"},{"title":"Australia’s first tap and go fast charging station up and running","url":"https://thedriven.io/2023/04/14/australias-first-tap-and-go-fast-charging-station-up-and-running/"},{"title":"Bicheno Town Centre","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/494062"},{"title":"Electrona Pty Ltd — Energy projects","url":"https://www.electrona.com.au/projects.html"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/"},{"title":"DC fast chargers in Tasmania","url":"https://www.aeva.asn.au/tas/dc-fast-chargers"},{"title":"Electric Vehicle ChargeSmart Grants","url":"https://recfit.tas.gov.au/grants_programs/chargesmart_grants"},{"title":"Tasmanian Fast / Ultra Fast chargers","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/tasmanian-fast-ultra-fast-chargers.98249/page-4"},{"title":"NRMA fast charging network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/nrma-fast-charging-network.100487/page-68"}]},"Electrona's Bicheno charger is open and you can pay by tapping a card, with no app needed. The Coles Bay charger is funded but still marked \"coming soon.\"\n\n**Bicheno (open since April 2023)**\n- **Location:** Foster Street, Bicheno, Tasmania (near IGA), station ID BCHNO001.\n- **Payment without an app:** You start a charge on the touch screen and pay with your credit card, with no app needed. The terminal takes credit cards, debit cards and NFC devices, but only Visa and Mastercard.\n- **Steps:** Plug a DC cable into the car (or use your own AC cable in the right-hand socket), tap the touch screen, choose \"Card Payment\" and then \"Start Charge\", and tap your card or phone on the reader.\n- **App or RFID backup:** If the card terminal gives you trouble, or you'd rather use an app, Wevolt works as an alternative and is on the App Store and Google Play. An RFID card also works. You can check availability in the Wevolt app or the Charge@Large app.\n- **Pricing (may change):** a $50 pre-authorisation that settles to the amount you actually used once your bank processes it. DC (CCS/CHAdeMO) costs $3 per session plus $0.64 per kWh; AC Type 2 costs $1 per session plus $0.64 per kWh. According to PlugShare, DC charging is capped at 2 hours, and a $0.50/minute idle fee applies after that.\n- **Hardware:** a Circontrol Raption with 50kW DC and 12kW AC, which can charge one car on DC and another on AC Type 2 at the same time.\n\n**Coles Bay (not open yet)**\n- Electrona's website lists Coles Bay and Orford as coming soon.\n- Under the Tasmanian Government's ChargeSmart 3 (2025) grants, Electrona Pty Ltd received $46,000 for Coles Bay. A June 2025 update from Electrona says it is bringing new fast chargers to Port Arthur, Bothwell, Coles Bay, and Orford.\n- I didn't find an opening date or confirmed payment methods for Coles Bay. Electrona's other sites suggest it will probably take cards and Wevolt too, but that isn't confirmed.\n\nElectrona's other open sites are Bothwell, Buckland, Huonville and Port Arthur."],"durationSeconds":11.064493876999993,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fm9FTohaya2A6vAknMw2B9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
