{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5rzsW9UK8iuYaEMJToDZm","type":"tool_result","content":"I can't reproduce the full file word for word because of the quoting limits, but here is a summary of the wevolt.com.au robots.txt.\n\n**Overall policy**\n- All crawlers are allowed by default, since search indexing brings in leads.\n- The core idea is to \"block AI *training* crawlers. Allow AI *answer engines*.\"\n- Training bots give the site nothing back. Answer engines cite the site, which counts as discovery, the same reason Googlebot is allowed.\n\n**Deliberately allowed (not listed)**\n- OpenAI: OAI-SearchBot and ChatGPT-User\n- Perplexity: PerplexityBot and Perplexity-User\n- Anthropic: Claude-User and Claude-SearchBot\n- Google: Google-Extended, unblocked 2026-08-05. The file explains it controls both Gemini training and Gemini grounding, and the grounding side is worth keeping. Googlebot and AI Overviews were never affected by it.\n- Apple: Applebot, through the wildcard rule\n\n**Blocked from the entire site (Disallow: /)**\n- **OpenAI:** GPTBot\n- **Anthropic:** ClaudeBot, Claude-Web, anthropic-ai\n- **Apple:** Applebot-Extended (blocks training only, not search)\n- **Meta:** Meta-ExternalAgent (both capitalizations), Meta-ExternalFetcher, FacebookBot\n- **Common Crawl:** CCBot\n- **ByteDance:** Bytespider\n- **Amazon:** Amazonbot\n- **Cohere:** cohere-ai, cohere-training-data-crawler\n- **Allen Institute:** AI2Bot, Ai2Bot-Dolma\n- **Others:** Diffbot, Omgili, Omgilibot, Webzio-Extended, ImagesiftBot, img2dataset, YouBot, Timpibot, PetalBot, DataForSeoBot, Scrapy, ISSCyberRiskCrawler\n- **Kangaroo Bot:** listed under three spellings (\"Kangaroo Bot\", \"Kangaroo\", \"KangarooBot\"), because a token containing a space gets truncated by parsers.\n\n**Operational notes**\n- The file says robots.txt is advisory: reputable operators honour it, but aggressive scrapers ignore it.\n- Vercel Firewall's AI Bots ruleset handles enforcement at the edge. Its Deny mode would also block the allowed answer engines, so it stays in Log mode unless a custom WAF bypass rule exempts those user agents. Custom rules run before managed rulesets.\n\n**Sitemap:** https://wevolt.com.au/sitemap-index.xml"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"9fc6cf0a-584a-4934-a94f-8ca760adfe39","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:31:12.606Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4037,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"I can't reproduce the full file word for word because of the quoting limits, but here is a summary of the wevolt.com.au robots.txt.\n\n**Overall policy**\n- All crawlers are allowed by default, since search indexing brings in leads.\n- The core idea is to \"block AI *training* crawlers. Allow AI *answer engines*.\"\n- Training bots give the site nothing back. Answer engines cite the site, which counts as discovery, the same reason Googlebot is allowed.\n\n**Deliberately allowed (not listed)**\n- OpenAI: OAI-SearchBot and ChatGPT-User\n- Perplexity: PerplexityBot and Perplexity-User\n- Anthropic: Claude-User and Claude-SearchBot\n- Google: Google-Extended, unblocked 2026-08-05. The file explains it controls both Gemini training and Gemini grounding, and the grounding side is worth keeping. Googlebot and AI Overviews were never affected by it.\n- Apple: Applebot, through the wildcard rule\n\n**Blocked from the entire site (Disallow: /)**\n- **OpenAI:** GPTBot\n- **Anthropic:** ClaudeBot, Claude-Web, anthropic-ai\n- **Apple:** Applebot-Extended (blocks training only, not search)\n- **Meta:** Meta-ExternalAgent (both capitalizations), Meta-ExternalFetcher, FacebookBot\n- **Common Crawl:** CCBot\n- **ByteDance:** Bytespider\n- **Amazon:** Amazonbot\n- **Cohere:** cohere-ai, cohere-training-data-crawler\n- **Allen Institute:** AI2Bot, Ai2Bot-Dolma\n- **Others:** Diffbot, Omgili, Omgilibot, Webzio-Extended, ImagesiftBot, img2dataset, YouBot, Timpibot, PetalBot, DataForSeoBot, Scrapy, ISSCyberRiskCrawler\n- **Kangaroo Bot:** listed under three spellings (\"Kangaroo Bot\", \"Kangaroo\", \"KangarooBot\"), because a token containing a space gets truncated by parsers.\n\n**Operational notes**\n- The file says robots.txt is advisory: reputable operators honour it, but aggressive scrapers ignore it.\n- Vercel Firewall's AI Bots ruleset handles enforcement at the edge. Its Deny mode would also block the allowed answer engines, so it stays in Log mode unless a custom WAF bypass rule exempts those user agents. Custom rules run before managed rulesets.\n\n**Sitemap:** https://wevolt.com.au/sitemap-index.xml","durationMs":10813,"url":"https://wevolt.com.au/robots.txt"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S5rzsW9UK8iuYaEMJToDZm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
