{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012f81sqDkVJGDsFXmbYLBH5","type":"tool_result","content":"**Yes, this is a terms page:** Wevolt's Website Terms & Conditions, last updated July 2026.\n\n**No explicit restriction.** The page never mentions automated access, scraping, robots, crawlers or data extraction.\n\n**Clauses that could arguably apply indirectly:**\n\n- **Use of this website:** Users agree not to misuse the site or interfere with its operation, nor to \"attempt to access it in any way other than through the interface we provide.\" This could be read as limiting automated or non-standard access, but it doesn't name bots or scraping.\n- **Intellectual property:** Site content \"may not reproduce or reuse them without our permission.\" This limits reuse of extracted content rather than the act of collecting it.\n\nSeparate service agreements govern the Wevolt Hub, apps and platform, and those aren't shown here."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"5bf2c229-96e8-429f-8fb6-a687c623df25","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:31:24.717Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":22039,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Yes, this is a terms page:** Wevolt's Website Terms & Conditions, last updated July 2026.\n\n**No explicit restriction.** The page never mentions automated access, scraping, robots, crawlers or data extraction.\n\n**Clauses that could arguably apply indirectly:**\n\n- **Use of this website:** Users agree not to misuse the site or interfere with its operation, nor to \"attempt to access it in any way other than through the interface we provide.\" This could be read as limiting automated or non-standard access, but it doesn't name bots or scraping.\n- **Intellectual property:** Site content \"may not reproduce or reuse them without our permission.\" This limits reuse of extracted content rather than the act of collecting it.\n\nSeparate service agreements govern the Wevolt Hub, apps and platform, and those aren't shown here.","durationMs":4723,"url":"https://wevolt.com.au/terms"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012f81sqDkVJGDsFXmbYLBH5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Z5BqYUkEzuULX9fdHcohE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NRMA Electric Highway Tasmania chargers Chargefox app 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NRMA Electric Vehicle Fast Charger Network\",\"url\":\"https://jss.sitecore.prod.svc.mynrma.com.au/electric-vehicles/charging\"},{\"title\":\"NRMA fast charging network\",\"url\":\"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/nrma-fast-charging-network.100487/page-68\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Highway Tasmania - FAQs\",\"url\":\"https://electrichighwaytasmania.com.au/faqs/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Road Trip Australia: 6 Routes With Chargers That Work\",\"url\":\"https://torquepress.com/drives/ev-road-trip-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)\",\"url\":\"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/\"},{\"title\":\"DC (Fast) Charging in Tasmania\",\"url\":\"https://aeva.asn.au/tas/charge/\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/247644\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/243112\"},{\"title\":\"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You\",\"url\":\"https://www.plugshare.com/location/217292\"},{\"title\":\"84 EV Charging Stations in Tasmania — AU EV Charging Finder\",\"url\":\"https://ev-charging.rollersoft.com.au/state/tas\"}]\n\nI found a clear answer: NRMA owns Electric Highway Tasmania (EHT), and its sites are paid through the Chargefox app. None of the results gives a specific 2025 date for when NRMA bought the network.\n\n**Who owns it:** NRMA says \"We own Electric Highway Tasmania, adding to our growing network of chargers across the country.\" NRMA also says members can save on charging at selected Chargefox locations, and that the displayed price is valid when using the Chargefox app. A Tesla Motors Club forum post notes that NRMA owns all of EHT's charging sites, and real-time updates on individual chargers are in the Chargefox app.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- A road-trip guide from about 77 days ago says the RAA and Electric Highway Tasmania sites run through Chargefox. It also warns that Chargefox runs 83 per cent of Tasmania's chargers, so an app outage hurts more here than anywhere else in the country.\n- PlugShare listings for EHT sites say you can pay with the Chargefox app, an RFID card linked to your Chargefox account, or a credit card. Some sites have limited mobile reception, and you can use the free wifi to start a session in the app.\n- The Tasmanian EV association (AEVA) says the Chargefox app can be used at NRMA chargers, or you can use the NRMA app.\n- An older forum post says the NRMA app is the only way to get the NRMA member discount, and that through roaming you can pay with your Chargefox account through the Chargefox app or RFID card.\n\n**EHT FAQ:** The Chargefox app covers many more charger sites than EHT's, most of which don't take credit cards. If a charger won't start, you may have picked the wrong connector when starting the session on the credit card terminal or in the Chargefox app.\n\n**Sites and prices (third-party directory, may be out of date):** NRMA Deloraine in Elizabeth Town has 180 kW and costs $0.74/kWh. EHT Kingston has 120 kW and costs $0.40–0.50/kWh. EHT Oatlands has 80 kW. Several EHT sites have 50 kW, including Swansea, St Helens, Devonport, Burnie, Queenstown and Geeveston, with some charging 25c/kWh plus 25c/min .\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"60ffe961-30e3-40c9-aebf-931c21a8ccb9","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:31:29.662Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"NRMA Electric Highway Tasmania chargers Chargefox app 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019CfrjKSzheeeVSd1Z6SzGZ","content":[{"title":"NRMA Electric Vehicle Fast Charger Network","url":"https://jss.sitecore.prod.svc.mynrma.com.au/electric-vehicles/charging"},{"title":"NRMA fast charging network","url":"https://teslamotorsclub.com/tmc/threads/nrma-fast-charging-network.100487/page-68"},{"title":"Electric Highway Tasmania - FAQs","url":"https://electrichighwaytasmania.com.au/faqs/"},{"title":"EV Road Trip Australia: 6 Routes With Chargers That Work","url":"https://torquepress.com/drives/ev-road-trip-australia/"},{"title":"EV Charging Stations in Tasmania (67 sites)","url":"https://evchargeraustralia.com.au/charging/tasmania/"},{"title":"DC (Fast) Charging in Tasmania","url":"https://aeva.asn.au/tas/charge/"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/247644"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/243112"},{"title":"PlugShare - Find Electric Vehicle Charging Locations Near You","url":"https://www.plugshare.com/location/217292"},{"title":"84 EV Charging Stations in Tasmania — AU EV Charging Finder","url":"https://ev-charging.rollersoft.com.au/state/tas"}]},"I found a clear answer: NRMA owns Electric Highway Tasmania (EHT), and its sites are paid through the Chargefox app. None of the results gives a specific 2025 date for when NRMA bought the network.\n\n**Who owns it:** NRMA says \"We own Electric Highway Tasmania, adding to our growing network of chargers across the country.\" NRMA also says members can save on charging at selected Chargefox locations, and that the displayed price is valid when using the Chargefox app. A Tesla Motors Club forum post notes that NRMA owns all of EHT's charging sites, and real-time updates on individual chargers are in the Chargefox app.\n\n**How to pay:**\n- A road-trip guide from about 77 days ago says the RAA and Electric Highway Tasmania sites run through Chargefox. It also warns that Chargefox runs 83 per cent of Tasmania's chargers, so an app outage hurts more here than anywhere else in the country.\n- PlugShare listings for EHT sites say you can pay with the Chargefox app, an RFID card linked to your Chargefox account, or a credit card. Some sites have limited mobile reception, and you can use the free wifi to start a session in the app.\n- The Tasmanian EV association (AEVA) says the Chargefox app can be used at NRMA chargers, or you can use the NRMA app.\n- An older forum post says the NRMA app is the only way to get the NRMA member discount, and that through roaming you can pay with your Chargefox account through the Chargefox app or RFID card.\n\n**EHT FAQ:** The Chargefox app covers many more charger sites than EHT's, most of which don't take credit cards. If a charger won't start, you may have picked the wrong connector when starting the session on the credit card terminal or in the Chargefox app.\n\n**Sites and prices (third-party directory, may be out of date):** NRMA Deloraine in Elizabeth Town has 180 kW and costs $0.74/kWh. EHT Kingston has 120 kW and costs $0.40–0.50/kWh. EHT Oatlands has 80 kW. Several EHT sites have 50 kW, including Swansea, St Helens, Devonport, Burnie, Queenstown and Geeveston, with some charging 25c/kWh plus 25c/min ."],"durationSeconds":10.794249253999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013Z5BqYUkEzuULX9fdHcohE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
