{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PDktqcfbx4QCgmQcnc93sZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EV charging price increase Australia November 2026 Evie Chargefox NRMA Ampol per kWh\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia: Real Cost Per 100km\",\"url\":\"https://revolted.au/ev-charging-networks-australia-cost/\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Does It Cost to Charge an EV in Australia? (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://evcharginglocations.com.au/blog/ev-charging-cost-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"Public EV Charging Network Cost Comparison (Australia 2026) — EV Costs Comparison\",\"url\":\"https://www.evcostscomparison.com/public-charging\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Cost in Australia 2026 — by State · ev.care · ev.care\",\"url\":\"https://ev.care/en-au/ev-charging-cost/au\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Australia Complete Guide 2026 — Everything You Need to Know\",\"url\":\"https://evscout.com.au/blog/ev-charging-australia-guide\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Apps Australia 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-apps-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"State of Charge: The Complete Guide to Australia’s EV Charging Networks in 2026 - evee AU - Electric Car Rental\",\"url\":\"https://pages.evee.com.au/blog/state-of-charge-guide-australia-ev-charging-networks-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Electric Car Running Costs Australia 2026 — Complete Cost Breakdown\",\"url\":\"https://evscout.com.au/blog/electric-car-running-costs-australia\"},{\"title\":\"NRMA EV Charging Network: Cost and Locations\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/nrma/\"}]\n\nI didn't find any news of a price increase announced in November 2026. The results are mostly 2026 comparison guides, and their figures sometimes disagree.\n\n**Ampol AmpCharge:** Gridly (about 47 days old) says standard pricing has risen to 75 c/kWh, making it one of the most expensive networks, with the price increasing from 60 c/kWh (2023) to 69 c (2024) to 75 c (2026). A subscription from $2.99 per month reduces the per-kWh rate. An older source still lists 69c/kWh, with Ampol blaming energy costs, and says AmpolCard holders get 4c/kWh off.\n\n**Ampol buying Evie:** Ampol reported AmpCharge sessions up 116 percent in the first half of 2026. Evie said around 380,000 of the roughly 500,000 EVs on Australian roads are registered in its app (AAP, October 2026).\n\n**Evie:** Prices run 58c at 50 kW, up to 73c at 350 kW. Evie is also trialling contactless tap-and-go payment at select sites, at roughly 5c/kWh extra.\n\n**Chargefox:** About 59–79c/kWh. It's the largest network. Each site owner sets its own prices, and motoring club members get a discount.\n\n**NRMA:** Publicly listed prices are 69, 75 and 79 cents per kWh, with 75 cents the most common. Remote sites cost more; NRMA's own pricing update cites 99 cents per kWh at Erldunda in the Northern Territory. Members have had a flat 5c/kWh discount since August 2025, replacing the old 10 per cent discount. It only applies when paying through the My NRMA app or at an on-site card reader. One October 2026 guide still lists 60–71c with a 10% member discount, which looks out of date.\n\n**Gaps:** None of the results reports a specific price change in November 2026. Older guides from 2025 and early 2026 show lower prices (around 40–60c), so they're probably out of date. Another search, for example \"Evie Networks price change\" or \"Ampol Evie acquisition pricing\", might turn up direct news.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"665e0d0f-59de-46f1-8009-aef3d0a475c4","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:31:52.745Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EV charging price increase Australia November 2026 Evie Char