{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Na214FE3ohbbMeMvsM66AY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ampol AmpCharge price per kWh 2026 increase 75 cents\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AMPOL AmpCharge Subscription — Plans from $2.99/mo (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://subger.com/en/er/service/ampol-ampcharge\"},{\"title\":\"AmpCharge Expands to 4 More Shopping Centres in Australia\",\"url\":\"https://zecar.com/reviews/ampcharge-opens-at-4-more-shopping-centres-across-nsw-qld-and-vic\"},{\"title\":\"Ampol AmpCharge: Network Guide for EV Drivers\",\"url\":\"https://evroadside.com.au/networks/ampol-ampcharge/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia 2026 Compared\",\"url\":\"https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-charging-networks-australia/\"},{\"title\":\"EV Charging Networks Australia: Real Cost Per 100km\",\"url\":\"https://revolted.au/ev-charging-networks-australia-cost/\"},{\"title\":\"AmpolCard now includes AmpCharge\",\"url\":\"https://www.finder.com.au/news/ampolcard-now-includes-ampcharge-oct-2026\"},{\"title\":\"\\\"Pretty steep:\\\" Ampol increases fast-charging prices for EV drivers by 15% - The Driven IO\",\"url\":\"https://thedriven.io/2023/02/07/pretty-steep-ampol-increases-fast-charging-prices-for-ev-drivers-by-15/\"},{\"title\":\"20% off Ampol AmpCharge EV Charging (Excluding NT, SA, TAS) for 6 Months @ Ampol AmpCharge - OzBargain\",\"url\":\"https://www.ozbargain.com.au/node/975772\"},{\"title\":\"Ampol Electricity - anyone tried them? - Electricity - Energy\",\"url\":\"https://forums.whirlpool.net.au/archive/30x16jkq\"},{\"title\":\"Ampol EV Charging Guide: Everything You Need to Know in 2025 - EV Charger News\",\"url\":\"https://evcharger.news/ampol-ev-charging/\"}]\n\nI found no official Ampol announcement of a 75c/kWh price. The 75c figure comes from user reports and one comparison site. Ampol doesn't publish a price list, and the last rise that was officially reported was in 2023.\n\n**Evidence for 75c/kWh in 2026:**\n- Gridly's 2026 comparison (about 47 days old) says standard pricing has risen to 75 c/kWh, making it one of the most expensive networks. It describes the history as 60 c/kWh (2023) to 69 c (2024) to 75 c (2026). Note that this conflicts with other sources, which date the 69c rise to February 2023, not 2024.\n- In an OzBargain thread from 20/09/2026, users said they charge 75c/kWh around me. They also noted that a 20% off promotion brings it to 60c/kWh. One user reported that new ones on the M1 north of Sydney at Wyong are 90c/kWh.\n- Subger lists 2026 pricing as pay-per-charge from AUD 0.55-0.75/kWh. This looks like an aggregator site and may not be reliable.\n\n**Conflicting or older sources:**\n- EV Roadside (mid-2026) says Ampol doesn't publish a rate card at all; charging prices appear per site in the Ampol app. It says the last reported figure is 69c/kWh at many sites, which came from a February 2023 price rise, up from 60 cents.\n- Zecar (about 161 days ago) says AmpCharge currently charges $0.69 per kWh at public sites.\n- The official 2023 rise was covered by The Driven: Ampol has started to charge EV drivers $0.69/kWh which is up from $0.60/kWh, blamed on wholesale energy costs.\n\n**Discounts:**\n- Finder (October 2026) reports that AmpolCard holders receive a discount of 4c/kWh at all AmpCharge locations.\n- Gridly mentions a subscription from $2.99 per month that reduces the per-kWh rate.\n\n**Other context:** According to Gridly, Ampol reported AmpCharge sessions up 116 percent in the first half of 2026, and Ampol is buying Evie Networks.\n\n**Bottom line:** By late 2026, 75c/kWh looks like the common pay-as-you-go rate, and some new sites charge up to 90c/kWh. But no official price-rise announcement or major news report turned up. Prices differ by site, and the Ampol app is the only official place to check them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"paren