{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAKZTkAR5V11jXeMqfSt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I opened one pull request, `[prices] Add Exploren and Wevolt; …`. It adds two networks, routes the ten other unmatched operators to existing networks, and changes no typical prices. Every operator on today's list now has a decision. `format.mjs` and `validate.mjs` both pass.\n\n**Added as networks, with no typical price:** no source I could use gives a typical figure for either.\n- **Exploren** (33 fast sites) also covers Engie's chargers. Its `siteReading` is `forbidden`, because the workflow says Exploren's terms forbid automated reading. A comparison site gives only a range of $0.55–0.75 for its fast chargers.\n- **Wevolt** (4 fast sites) also covers Electrona's Tasmanian chargers. Its `siteReading` is `unchecked`: robots.txt allows my kind of fetch, but its terms say to use the site only \"through the interface we provide\".\n\n**Added to an existing network's list:**\n- **Chargefox:** Yurika and the Queensland Electric Super Highway, RAA, Electric Highway Tasmania, WA EV Network, Horizon Power and Woolworths. Each is paid through the Chargefox app, according to TMR, Queensland councils, raa.com.au, AEVA, Horizon Power and Chargefox's Woolworths release.\n- **Evie:** Charging the Regions. The councils' alliance that runs it says Evie operates and maintains its 23 fast sites.\n\n**Flagged in the pull request for a reviewer:**\n- **Over-matching:** the app matches by substring, so the short text `raa` could catch an unrelated site name. A Woolworths site run by another network might also be read as Chargefox.\n- **Engie:** its sites work with both Exploren and Chargefox. I chose Exploren because Exploren-run sites already carry the Engie name.\n- **Ampol:** a comparison blog and some forum users say its standard price is now 75c, up from 0.69. There's no official or news source, so I left it at 0.69. It's worth checking in the Ampol app.\n- **Pages I couldn't read:** mynrma.com.au and horizonpower.com.au refused the fetch. The Driven feed wasn't in the sources folder, so I opened no articles from it.\n\nI opened no issue: every network's price was last checked on 27 October 2026, well inside six months. The decision for each operator is saved in memory."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2364,"cache_read_input_tokens":73767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2364,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c59389d-e35a-4c8f-bb09-2fcfce2e7e03","uuid":"3a23f3bd-2ba5-4b2f-a184-efda9153dc89","timestamp":"2026-11-18T11:33:12.169Z","request_id":"req_011ChAKZTQLa3jL9TgcWUbBJ"}
